{title: Behold (Then Sings My Soul)}
{artist: Hillsong Worship}
{key: B}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[B]Behold the Father’s heart
The [E]mystery He lavishes on us
As [G#m]deep cries out to d[B]eep
Oh how desperately He [E]wants us
The [G#m]things of earth stand n[B]ext to Him
Like a candle to the [E]sun
Unfailing Fat[G#m]her
What c[F#]ompares to His G[E]reat love

{comment: Verse 2}
Behold His holy Son
The Lion and the Lamb given to us
The Word became a man
That my soul should know its Saviour
Forsaken for the sake of all mankind
Salvation is in His blood
Jesus Messiah
The righteous died for love
It wasn’t over
For He is the risen One

{comment: Chorus}
Then sings my [B]soul
Then sings my [G#m]soul
